My last game saw unremarkable demons summon Jubilex (early) and 
Yeenoghu. Of course we can't stop demons from using a lifeline and 
calling for a friend; but, shouldn't Demonbane have an effect on this 
process?

An explorer cannot teleport onto a square already occupied, and attempts 
to do so cause a random teleport. I suggest Demonbane prevent summoned 
demons from appearing in a 3x3 area around the Demonbane wielder. The 
demon would arrive in a random location on the level outside the 3x3 
square -- just like a random teleport.

Since the probability of a demon summoning one of the major demons is 
small, the possibility of a demon being summoned while the explorer is 
weilding Demonbane would be even more remote. Just another little twist 
to increase the games complexity.


